* Behavioral RP2350 + firmware, as far as the power button can see it.
*
* Only the pins on the button's nets are modelled, with the numbers the
* RP2350 datasheet gives (design/datasheets/RP2350.pdf):
*   QSPI_SS (CSn): bootrom sets it "output disabled, pulled high" and
*     samples it "shortly after reset" (s5.2.8). Pull-up RPU 32-86k at
*     IOVDD 3.3V (Table 1683). Low <= 0.8V, high >= 2.0V.
*   RUN: global asynchronous reset, low = reset (pin table).
*   GPIO20/21: reset state is pull-down enabled; RPD 36-113k (Table 1683).
*   POR releases once DVDD passes ~0.96V (s7.6.1); DVDD comes from the
*     on-chip regulator, whose VREG_VIN needs >= 2.7V (s7.1), so "chip
*     alive" is 3V3 > 2.7V (2.5V falling). (Was 1.8V until the independent
*     review flagged it as unphysical.)
*
* The bootrom's sample time after reset is not specified, so it is a
* corner parameter (t_samp). Firmware is scenario stimulus, not the
* device under test: fwreq (0/1) says whether firmware WANTS PWR_HOLD
* high, and it only gets to drive the pin once it is running, i.e.
* t_fw after reset release AND the bootrom did not take the BOOTSEL path.
*
* Observation nodes (wrdata these): act, smp, bsel, fwon.


.subckt RP2350 VDD RUN CSN PWR_HOLD BTN FWREQ act smp bsel fwon
* --- reset: power OK and RUN high ---
Bpw pw0 0 V = V(VDD) > (V(pw) > 0.5 ? 2.5 : 2.7) ? 1 : 0
Rpw pw0 pw 1k
Cpw pw 0 1n
Brn rn0 0 V = V(RUN) > (V(rn) > 0.5 ? 0.8 : 2.0) ? 1 : 0
Rrn rn0 rn 1k
Crn rn 0 1n
Bact act 0 V = V(pw) * V(rn)

* --- digital: sample CSn t_samp after reset release; latch BOOTSEL ---
Acsl [act] [d_act] abr
Bcs cslo 0 V = V(CSN) < 1.4 ? 1 : 0
Acs2 [cslo] [d_cslo] abr
Afw2 [FWREQ] [d_req] abr
.model abr adc_bridge(in_low=0.45 in_high=0.55)
Adly d_act d_smp dly_s
.model dly_s d_buffer(rise_delay={t_samp} fall_delay=1n)
Anrst d_act d_rst inv
.model inv d_inverter(rise_delay=1n fall_delay=1n)
Aff d_cslo d_smp null d_rst d_bsel d_bsel_n dff
.model dff d_dff(clk_delay=1n set_delay=1n reset_delay=1n)
Afwd d_act d_fwt dly_f
.model dly_f d_buffer(rise_delay={t_fw} fall_delay=1n)
Axip d_smp d_xipt dly_x
.model dly_x d_buffer(rise_delay=200u fall_delay=1n)
Aand1 [d_fwt d_bsel_n] d_fwon and2
Aand2 [d_xipt d_bsel_n] d_xip and2
Aand3 [d_fwon d_req] d_hold and2
.model and2 d_and(rise_delay=1n fall_delay=1n)
Adac [d_smp d_bsel d_fwon d_xip d_hold] [smp bsel fwon xip hold] dac1
.model dac1 dac_bridge(out_low=0 out_high=1 t_rise=1u t_fall=1u)

* --- pins ---
* CSn: bootrom pull-up always; XIP drives it high (40 ohm) once flash boot runs
Rpu VDD CSN {rpu}
Bxip 0 CSN I = V(xip) * (V(VDD) - V(CSN)) / 40
Ccs CSN 0 5p
* PWR_HOLD (GPIO20): reset pull-down; firmware drives it high (50 ohm)
Rpd20 PWR_HOLD 0 {rpd}
Bhold 0 PWR_HOLD I = V(hold) * (V(VDD) - V(PWR_HOLD)) / 50
* BTN (GPIO21): input, reset pull-down
Rpd21 BTN 0 {rpd}
* RUN: input only (R2 on the board is the pull-up)
Crun RUN 0 5p
* supply current: ~20mA running, ~1mA in reset; 100k = unpowered leakage
Roff VDD 0 100k
Bload VDD 0 I = V(VDD) > 0.3 ? (V(act) * 0.020 + 0.001) * min(1, V(VDD) / 3.0) : 0
.ends RP2350
